# TeaVM bundle size budget: max allowed bytes per generated bundle.
# The build FAILS when a bundle exceeds these. After a deliberate size
# change, regenerate with the updateBundleBudget task and commit.
# measured= is the size this ceiling was derived from, so the next
# breach can report how much the bundle GREW since this baseline.
# 2026-09-28: hawkeye's render-error containment gives every generated template region its own catch (the
# generated template packages dominate the growth): raw 6046963 -> 6572760, gzip 1425643 -> 1523166.
# 2026-10-01: module-fit stages 1-2 (principal kinds, registries, the common activity action members and their
# legacy keys in the StoredIds holders): raw 6572760 -> 6746997, gzip 1523166 -> 1599874.
# 2026-10-06: R7c consumer landing against the rebased framework chain, including current CMS/auth surfaces and
# the expanded DRY admission/parser. Measured 7505575 raw / 1779877 gzip (+384634 / +93020 from the baseline).
# Generated CMS +48948, plumage tags +42120, auth tags +34185 and DRY +33524. Class attribution includes CMS
# HawkeyeClassSerializers +26412, Tpl_ZaRecordSharing +24465, auth HawkeyeClassSerializers +13691,
# Parser +13161, Tpl_PlSelect +12079 and ZaRecordSharingImpl +9381. Keep the standard 5 percent headroom.
# 2026-10-08: a VM's console is a zenit-kvm screen (<kvm-screen>, hh-vm-screen) instead of plumage's
# FramebufferWire, plus the template work since 2026-10-06: raw 7505575 -> 7829863, gzip 1779877 -> 1862955.
# Generated templates +130904, unmapped +87242, zenit-kvm +64359 (ScreenMessage +25032, BrowserScreenViewer
# +13667, ScreenCodec +9827); TeaVM's BigDecimal/BigInteger fell out (-19621). Standard 5 percent headroom.
cms.js.raw=8221357 measured=7829863
cms.js.gzip=1956103 measured=1862955
